            {
              "text": "Found a prior thread on the dev forum: \"VSCode TS server can't find react types after restart — how do you reset it?\" (p002, by priya.r). It describes exactly your error.\n\nFen Wu's fix:\n1) rm -rf node_modules/.cache/typescript\n2) If that isn't enough, run pnpm install --force (or npm install / yarn install --force).\n3) In VSCode, run Cmd+Shift+P -> \"TypeScript: Restart TS Server\".\n\nJin Kim added two more things to check:\n- Cmd+Shift+P -> \"TypeScript: Select TypeScript Version\" -> \"Use Workspace Version\". A mismatch with VSCode's bundled TS causes phantom errors.\n- Check tsconfig.json: make sure baseUrl is set correctly if you use path aliases.\n\nThere's also a pinned urgent post (p001) from marcus.l with the same issue. I haven't posted anything on the forum."
            }
          ],
